# Web app settings. Copy to apps/web/.env.local for `next dev`.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JavaScript at BUILD time, so for a
# deployment they must be present in the environment of the build
# (`pnpm --filter @ahemads-restro/web deploy:staging`, `build:cf`, `preview`),
# for example in apps/web/.env.production.local or the CI job's environment.
# Setting them on the running Worker afterwards has no effect. Never commit
# real values.
#
# The site variables below are commented out on purpose: an EMPTY value
# (NAME=) counts as "set" and replaces the built-in fallback with an empty
# string. Uncomment a line only when you have a real value for it.

# --- Local development only (`next dev`, port 1995) -------------------------
# The deployed web Worker forwards /api/* to the API Worker over a service
# binding and needs neither of these.

# Where `next dev` proxies /api/* (the API's `wrangler dev`).
API_DEV_URL=http://localhost:8787

# `next dev` cannot proxy WebSocket upgrades, so the realtime socket goes
# straight to the API's wrangler dev. Use "localhost" (not 127.0.0.1) so the
# session cookie, which is scoped to the host, is sent along.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8787

# --- Public marketing site (/en, /ar) ---------------------------------------

# Canonical origin of the site, without a trailing slash, e.g.
# https://www.example.com. Used for canonical URLs, hreflang, Open Graph,
# sitemap.xml and robots.txt. Falls back to http://localhost:1995, so it MUST
# be set for any public build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Google Analytics 4 measurement id. Optional. Analytics only loads when this
# is set AND the visitor accepts the consent banner. Leave unset until the
# owner has created a GA4 property; never commit someone else's id.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Google Search Console HTML-tag verification token (only the content="..."
# value of the google-site-verification meta tag). Optional; verifying the
# domain through DNS needs nothing here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GSC_VERIFICATION=

# Public support e-mail address shown in the site footer. Optional; no
# address is shown while it is unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# Public URL of THIS deployment's source code (AGPL-3.0 section 13 source
# offer), linked from the site footer. While unset the footer links to the
# upstream Nodedr OrderRestro repository, which does not contain this
# edition's changes, so set it before the site goes public.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOURCE_CODE_URL=
